  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Stablecoin market cap fell 5.4% over 30D:</strong> Stablecoin market cap at $273.87B (5.4% lower over 30D). Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/markets/stablecoin-market-shrinks-about-17-billion-in-30-days\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Stablecoin Market Shrinks About $17 Billion in 30 Days</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Stablecoin market structure remains concentration-led:</strong> leadership is still defined by a small set of large issuers/platforms; share shifts matter as much as aggregate market-cap growth. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/converge/tradfi-and-fintech/deel-launches-stablecoin-spending-card-in-26-markets\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Deel Launches Stablecoin Spending Card in 26 Markets</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Bank rails are pushing stablecoins into treasury workflows:</strong> That pushes demand toward treasury and settlement use cases, not only exchange trading liquidity. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/11/24/south-korea-regulator-backs-bank-controlled-stablecoins-after-months-of-dispute\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">South Korea regulator backs bank-controlled stablecoins after months of dispute</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
